 "weather": {
  "_about": "(0.4.7, gamefixes: every weather polished) the weather heard: looped beds (sounds/elements: real recordings cut into seamless loops by work/gen47/hqsnd/build_sounds.py, sources in sounds/CREDITS.txt) each brought up by the part of the weather it follows ('rain', 'wind', 'hail', 'snow', 'sand', 'drift', 'storm', or two multiplied: 'snow*wind') - silent below 'from', full at 'full', and faded out again from 'fadeFrom' to 'fadeTo' where a heavier bed takes over; 'gain' is its loudness when full. Under a roof every bed is heard at 'indoors' (the rain on the roof), underground at 'underground'; each eases to its level over 'fade' seconds. (0.4.8) The rain is a wash over the land (the beds: light rain in a wood under rain on leaves; a downpour on leaves), a 'roof' bed of rain drumming overhead heard only under a roof (the open air's beds are dulled through the walls by the mixer), and 'drops': single recorded drops scattered round the listener, 'rate' a second at full rain between 'near' and 'far' metres, each on what it lands on ('surfaces': its files, 'gain', 'pitch', or 'as' another surface's bank) and heard within 'range'.",
